NNAAMMEE
       showq - list the Postfix mail queue

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       sshhoowwqq [generic Postfix daemon options]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  sshhoowwqq(8) daemon reports the Postfix mail queue status.  The output
       is meant to be formatted by the postqueue(1) command,  as  it  emulates
       the Sendmail ‘mailq’ command.

       The  sshhoowwqq(8)  daemon  can also be run in stand-alone mode by the supe‐
       ruser. This mode of operation is used to emulate  the  ‘mailq’  command
       while the Postfix mail system is down.

SSEECCUURRIITTYY
       The  sshhoowwqq(8)  daemon  can run in a chroot jail at fixed low privilege,
       and takes no input from the client. Its service port is  accessible  to
       local  untrusted  users, so the service can be susceptible to denial of
       service attacks.

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
       None. The sshhoowwqq(8) daemon does not interact with the outside world.

DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
       Problems and transactions are logged to ssyyssllooggdd(8) or ppoossttllooggdd(8).

